: initial"><SPAN=20
style=3D"FONT-SIZE: 12pt; COLOR: black">Epidemiology seeks to determin=
e=20
associations between exposure risk and disease that are spatially depe=
ndent.=20
Public health focuses on the health of populations rather than of indi=
viduals=20
and focuses more on prevention of health problems. These efforts fall =
naturally=20
within the domain of problems requiring use of spatial analysis as par=
t of the=20
solution, and GIS and other spatial analysis tools are therefore recog=
nized as=20
providing potentially transformational capabilities for Epidemiology a=
nd public=20
health efforts.</SPAN></P>
